      "writtenOn": "2022-02-08T12:54:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So since you these referencing GPIOs directly, you should be able to use\nGPIO_DT_SPEC_GET directly without having to redefine the macro, unless you\nare expecting the GPIO flags to also include flags past the \u0027usual\u0027 Zephyr GPIO flags (like including GPIO_INPUT etc.).\nHowever I see where you are configuring the pins, you are including the\nINPUT/OUTPUT flags, so as far as I can see, it is quite OK to use the standard macro (if you were using a reference to an EC \u0027named-gpio\u0027, this wouldn\u0027t be the case, since that holds a 32 bit value for the flags).",
      "revId": "729e4e46e41a1b1bcbb2af5b40d4678101a6f7cd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
